   DESCENDANT COMBINATOR
   ------------------------------------------------------

   The descendant combinator in CSS is used to select 
   elements that are inside another element, at any depth.

   It works by placing a SPACE between two selectors.

   ✔ Syntax:
       parent child

   ✔ Meaning:
       Selects all elements that match "child" which are 
       located anywhere inside the element matching "parent".

   It does NOT matter whether the child is:
       • a direct child
       • a grandchild
       • nested deeply inside

   If it is inside, it will be selected.

   ------------------------------------------------------
   Example:
       div p {
           color: blue;
       }

   This means:
       • Select all <p> elements
       • That are inside a <div>, at any level
       • Works even if <p> is 2, 3, or 10 levels deep

   HTML Example:
       <div>
           <p>Direct child → selected</p>

           <section>
               <p>Grandchild → also selected</p>
           </section>
       </div>

       <p>Outside the div → NOT selected</p>
